@startuml eof-audit-pipeline
title "eof-audit" step (skill analyse-parcours) — Tool pipeline -> EOF reference

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  BorderColor #5BA1BC
  FontColor #1C2856
  DiamondBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  DiamondBorderColor #5BA1BC
}
skinparam ArrowColor #5BA1BC
skinparam ActivityBarColor #5BA1BC
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9BD0DD
skinparam PartitionBackgroundColor #ECECF2
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #5BA1BC

start

partition "**Already collected sources** (base journey + e-footprint)" {
  :env-data.json
  (device_mix, servers[], traffic, tech_stack...);
  :audit/har-analysis.json
  (domains, http_codes, duplicate_urls);
  :audit/coverage-analysis.json
  (unused JS/CSS per page);
  :cwv.json
  (LCP/INP/CLS — CrUX or PageSpeed lab);
}

note right #C8E6C9
  cwv.json extended in Phase 1 (2026-09-03):
  collect_cwv_pagespeed.py additionally requests
  the "accessibility" and
  "best-practices" categories (same PageSpeed API
  call, no extra network cost) ->
  accessibility_score_pct / best_practices_score_pct
end note

partition "**Phase 1 extractors** (new, 2026-09-03)" {
  :parse_html_criteria.py
  live re-fetch of already audited pages
  (the captured .har does not contain the
  HTML/CSS bodies — verified: 46/311 entries
  with a body, none of them HTML/CSS pages)
  -> html-css-criteria.json;
  :analyze_security_headers.py
  local security score (securityheaders.com type)
  from the headers already in the .har
  -> security-headers-analysis.json;
  :scan_wellknown.py
  direct fetch security.txt / robots.txt /
  sitemap.xml (3 public HTTP requests)
  -> wellknown-scan.json;
}

note right
  Pitfall encountered and fixed on octo.com:
  robots.txt AND sitemap.xml returned a
  status 200 but the SPA fallback HTML
  (catch-all routing), not the requested
  resource -> detection added so a false
  "present" is not counted.
end note

partition "**run_eof.py** (deterministic, no LLM calculation)" {
  :Load eof-reference.json
  (54 criteria + 16 Quick diagnostic,
  produced by the eof skill, NEVER regenerated here);
  :Load the 7 sources above
  into a single data{} dict;
  if (Rule "automatable" settles
  without ambiguity ?) then (yes)
    :Tick one option of the 5-choice
    menu (including "🤔 To be assessed" if
    ambiguous zone — still an explicit answer,
    not an "I don't know");
  else (no / category "partial")
    :Display a contextual hint in the appendix
    (confidence low/medium, never ticked);
  endif
  :Compute the scores per dimension
  (weighted average over the real answers);
}

note right #C8E6C9
  Anti-fabrication policy unchanged:
  7 detailed automatable criteria (was 4)
  + 11 "partial" hints (was 6) after Phase 1.
  36 criteria remain "I don't know"
  (organizational/product questions).
end note

:-> eof-audit-results.json
(summary, consumed by generate_report_html.py);
:-> eof-filled.md
(full reference, answer/context + source);
:-> eof-radar-<domain>.svg
(6-dimension radar, "N/A" if no answer);

stop

@enduml
